=========================================================================================================
15_karimova_reproduction.py — Reproduction of the original deep-network results (TensorFlow environment)
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  The original study reports R2 = 0.75 for its baseline network, 0.82 after keeping the
  descriptors with a positive         permutation importance, and 0.85 after adding Gaussian-noise
  copies of the training molecules. Each value comes from one         execution of a notebook on
  one train/test split. Part 15a runs those notebooks again, unchanged, and compares the
  printed R2 with the published notebooks. Part 15b re-runs the same protocol, step by step, with
  several random seeds,         to see how much these values move from one execution to the next.
  Both parts use the original protocol, including the         choices that the next step (16)
  examines as possible information leaks.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
